      <Placemark>
        <description>http://www.aqua.org/

Plan on spending at least a couple of hours or more, especially if you include the dolphin show - high recommended.  In the summer, the lines to buy tickets get long (try buying online) and may not provide immediate entry.  On the busiest days (weekends usually), you may have to wait several hours after your ticket purchase before you can enter.  Plan on going early and be prepared to find something else to do for a while until your time to enter.  It still well worth it if you&apos;re prepared.</description>
        <name>National Aquarium at Baltimore</name>
        <View>
          <longitude>-76.60786099605816</longitude>
          <latitude>39.28492634228216</latitude>
          <range>333.1631352165023</range>
          <tilt>1.02814324728673e-009</tilt>
          <heading>0.03694824360656396</heading>
        </View>
        <visibility>1</visibility>
        <styleUrl>#cloned8</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-76.60815282644298,39.28479903804354,27.49588277066488</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <description>Several types of paddle (and electric) boats for rent at the floating docks on either side of the World Trade Center building.  You&apos;re generally restricted to the part of the harbor between the USS Constellation pier and the National Aquarium pier - so don&apos;t plan on using these as your means of transportation to points around the harbor.</description>
        <name>Paddleboats</name>
        <View>
          <longitude>-76.60849831193912</longitude>
          <latitude>39.28570111871262</latitude>
